Q3. Internal Working of ArrayList ?
 - Data structure :
                      a. Internally, ArrayList uses a dynamic array (not a fixed-size array). It means elements are stored contiguously in memory like a normal array
 - Dynamic resizing :
                      a. When ArrayList reaches its current capacity, it automatically increases the size.
                      b. Default growth: new capacity = old capacity + (old capacity / 2) (approx 1.5 times).
 - Adding elements :
                      a. add(element) → adds at the end of the array.
                      b. add(index, element) → shifts elements to the right to insert at given index.
- Removing elements :
                      a. remove(index) → shifts all elements to the left to fill the gap.
                      b. This is O(n) operation in the worst case.
 - Capacity vs Size :
                      a. Capacity → total length of internal array.
                      b. Size → number of elements actually present.
                      c. Default constructor → 10 elements.




